---
title: "SD-08 Tag, Release and Deploy (UML Sequence Diagram)"
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor D as Developer
  participant A as Anvil server
  participant RW as Runner (windows)
  participant RL as Runner (linux)
  participant RD as Runner (deploy, prod server)
  actor O as Repository Admin

  D->>A: git push origin v1.4.0
  A->>A: git.tag.created → trigger matches tags: [v*]
  par build on both OSes
    A->>RW: job build-windows
    RW->>A: upload artifact app-windows
  and
    A->>RL: job build-linux
    RL->>A: upload artifact app-linux
  end
  A->>RL: job release (needs both builds)
  RL->>A: download artifacts
  RL->>A: POST /releases {tag_name: v1.4.0}
  RL->>A: POST /releases/{id}/assets (zip, tar.gz)
  A->>A: Publish(release.published)
  A-->>O: deploy job waiting (when: manual)
  O->>A: click "Run" on deploy job
  A->>RD: job deploy (environment: production)
  A->>A: deployments row: in_progress
  RD->>A: GET /releases/latest/assets/app-linux.tar.gz
  RD->>RD: stop service, unpack, start, health check /healthz
  alt health check fails
    RD->>RD: roll back to previous version
    RD->>A: finish failure
    A->>A: deployment: failure
  else healthy
    RD->>A: finish success
    A->>A: deployment: success (production = v1.4.0)
  end
